# Project Architecture & UML Documentation

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the **Drone Detection & Surveillance System** architecture through various UML diagrams.

---

## 1. Use Case Diagram
Describes the functional requirements and technical interactions between the user and the system components.

```mermaid
useCaseDiagram
    actor "Surveillance Operator" as User
    actor "GPS Satellite" as GPS
    actor "External Camera" as Camera
    
    package "Drone Detection System" {
        usecase "Monitor Live Feed" as UC1
        usecase "Upload Image/Video" as UC2
        usecase "Detect & Classify Drones" as UC3
        usecase "Trigger GPS Alerts" as UC4
        usecase "Manage Detection Archive" as UC5
    }
    
    database "MongoDB" as DB
    
    User --> UC1
    User --> UC2
    User --> UC5
    
    UC1 --> Camera
    UC1 ..> UC3 : "include"
    UC2 ..> UC3 : "include"
    UC3 ..> UC4 : "extend"
    UC4 --> GPS
    
    UC3 --> DB : "Store Log"
    UC5 --> DB : "Query/Delete"
```

---

## 2. Class Diagram
Visualizes the structural components of the Python/Flask backend and their relationships.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class FlaskApp {
        +route_index()
        +route_live_page()
        +route_detect_image()
        +route_detect_video()
        +route_history()
    }
    
    class YOLODetector {
        -model: YOLO
        +detect(frame) : results
        +draw_detections(frame, results)
    }
    
    class MongoDBManager {
        -client: MongoClient
        -db: drones_db
        +insert_detection(record)
        +fetch_history()
        +delete_record(id)
    }
    
    class SurveillanceLogic {
        -drone_alert_status: dict
        -current_gps: dict
        +update_location(lat, lon)
        +save_with_cooldown(frame, details)
    }
    
    class WebInterface {
        <<Template>>
        +layout.html
        +index.html
        +live.html
        +history.html
    }
    
    FlaskApp --> YOLODetector : Uses
    FlaskApp --> MongoDBManager : Persists
    FlaskApp --> SurveillanceLogic : Coordinates
    WebInterface ..> FlaskApp : Interacts
```

---

## 3. Sequence Diagram (Detection Flow)
Illustrates the time-ordered interaction for a successful drone detection event.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Browser
    participant Flask as Flask Server
    participant YOLO as YOLO11 Model
    participant DB as MongoDB
    
    User->>Browser: Start Live Surveillance
    Browser->>Flask: Send Video Frame (Base64)
    Flask->>YOLO: run_inference(frame)
    YOLO-->>Flask: List[Boxes, Conf, Class]
    
    alt Drone Detected
        Flask->>Flask: Draw Bounding Boxes
        Flask->>Flask: Check Save Cooldown
        alt Cooldown Expired
            Flask->>DB: Store Detection + GPS + Path
            DB-->>Flask: Success (ID)
            Flask->>Flask: Save JPG to /static/detections
        end
        Flask-->>Browser: Annotated Frame + JSON ALERT
        Browser->>User: Display Alert & Trigger Alarm
    else No Drone
        Flask-->>Browser: Clean Frame
    end
```

---

## 4. Activity Diagram (System Logic)
Shows the control flow of the application from startup to background monitoring.

```mermaid
activityDiagram
    start
    :Initialize Flask & YOLO Model;
    :Connect to MongoDB;
    if (Connection Successful?) then (yes)
        :Enable History Storage;
    else (no)
        :Disable History / Log Error;
    endif
    
    fork
        :Listen for Dashboard Requests;
    fork again
        :Process Live Surveillance Stream;
        while (Stream Active?)
            :Capture Frame;
            :Run YOLO Inference;
            if (Drone Above Threshold?) then (yes)
                :Generate Alert Record;
                :Save to Archive (with cooldown);
                :Notify Frontend;
            else (no)
                :Continue Monitoring;
            endif
        endwhile
    end fork
    stop
```

---

## 5. System Architecture (High Level)
A block diagram of the integrated technology stack.

```mermaid
graph TD
    UI[Frontend: HTML5/CSS/JS] <--> API[Flask Backend API]
    API <--> ML[YOLOv11 Detection Engine]
    API <--> MDB[(MongoDB Archive)]
    API <--> FS[Local Filesystem: Image Storage]
    
    GPS[Browser GPS API] --> UI
    CAM[Device Camera] --> UI
    
    subgraph "Solar Surveillance Theme"
        UI
    end
```
